30,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,Transport costs vary wildly depending on distance. Staying local or nearby is the only way to keep the budget stable.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Public bookings are a bureaucratic nightmare, and cooking for ourselves is too much of a burden on the organizers.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Minako,,"It seems we only bond when we stay together. Also, if we don't make the camp appealing, people just quit the club.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I've found that inland centers can be cramped and restrictive, and our own hall is already overbooked during the vacation.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"A whole-building let is risky because late cancellations penalize everyone. Also, many members can't commute to campus daily.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, if public bookings are difficult, maybe a private lodge is better, provided the cost is fixed.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, as long as the lodge provides meals. We cannot have the organizers spending their training time in the kitchen.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Jonathan, if the hall is full and inland centers are too restrictive, the Coastal Lodge might be the best compromise.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I agree. Quality sleep is essential for the final day's performance, and a private building sounds more peaceful.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Ryuji, the ""fixed cost"" of a lodge is a trap. If someone drops out, the remaining members pay the difference.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, that is a risk, but the transport cost for a distant lodge might be lower than a public center if we manage it.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Toshio,,I cannot support any option that requires a nine-page lottery application or student-led cooking.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Minako,,"If we stay on campus, we lose the social bonding. We need a place where everyone sleeps under one roof.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,The campus option seems impossible if the training times are split between early mornings and late nights.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"If we stay on campus, a third of the members still need paid beds. It doesn't actually save that much.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,It seems the Campus Intensive is impractical due to the timetable and commute.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Toshio,,And the Mountain Centre is too much paperwork and potential labor.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Minako,,"The Coastal Lodge allows us to stay together, which is vital for the club's unity.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. It avoids the overcrowding of the inland centers and the chaos of the campus hall.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I still dislike the financial risk of the lodge, but the other options are logically flawed.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
